+/**
+ * The MEASURED host gate: a guest (or measured host runtime) checks its OWN host id. It reports `serving: false` on any
+ * refusal or undecided state after the grace, and the caller stops admitting new work (and, for a ban, stops serving).
+ * graceMs keeps a running guest serving through transient RPC/mirror loss (never through an explicit ban).
